<title>CANADA: Canada commission soft spring wheat quality data.</title>
<headline>Canada commission soft spring wheat quality data.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Grain Commission on Thursday detailed preliminary milling and baking test</p>
<p>results for No1 Canada Western Soft White Spring Wheat.</p>
<p>PRELIMINARY DATA ON No1 Canada Western Soft White Spring Wheat</p>
<p>Quality Parameters		 1996	     1995</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p>  Test weight (kg/hl)	    82.5	     81.5</p>
<p>  Weight per 1,000 kernels, g  37.3	     36.1</p>
<p>  Protein Content (pct)	  10.4	     10.2</p>
<p>  Dry Matter Protein (pct)     12.0	     11.8</p>
<p>  Ash Content (pct)		 1.66	     1.50</p>
<p>  Alpha-amylase Activity unit/g17.0	     15.0</p>
<p>  Falling Number		  335		330</p>
<p>  Flour Yield (pct)		77.2	     77.4</p>
<p>  PSI (pct)			  68		 71</p>
<p>FLOUR</p>
<p>  Protein Content (pct)	   9.4		9.3</p>
<p>  Wet Gluten Content (pct)     25.8	     29.0</p>
<p>  Ash Content (pct)		 0.54	     0.53</p>
<p>  Grade Colour, K-J units	-0.1	     -0.1</p>
<p>  AGTRON Colour (pct)	    63		 63</p>
<p>  Starch damage, Megazyme units 3.1	     n/a</p>
<p>  Starch damage, AACC units     4.5		5.2</p>
<p>  Alpha-amylase Activity unit/g 1.5		4.0</p>
<p>  Amylograph Peak Viscosity, BU 540		335</p>
<p>  Maltose Value, g/100 g	  1.2		1.3</p>
<p>  Zeleny Sedimentation, mL     19		 17</p>
<p>  Flour Akaline Water Retention64.2	     61.0</p>
<p>FARINOGRAM</p>
<p>  Absorption (pct)		 54.6	     55.4</p>
<p>  Development Time, mins.	 1.25	     1.25</p>
<p>  Mixing Tolerance Index, BU  215		180</p>
<p>  Stability, mins.		  1.00	     1.50</p>
<p>N.B.: unless otherwise noted, data based on 13.5 pct wheat</p>
<p>moisture and 14.0 pct flour moisture.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
